#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119564 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"}] :question/id #uuid "219df52e-8833-58df-8a2f-ee53cfed5640" :question/math-academy-id "e-3135" :question/problem "Consider the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = -\\dfrac{4}{5}\\sin{s}\\,\\mathbf i+\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sin{s}\\, \\mathbf j + \\cos{s}\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(s)$ are both parametrized by the arc length $s,$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $\\mathbf T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)k \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+0\\,j-k \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖=‖-k‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119565 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"}] :question/id #uuid "ea963bd4-6c5b-5385-8efc-dcd4de104da0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3140" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(t) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin t, \\:2\\cos t \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\mathbf T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf \\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\left\\| \\mathbf T'(t) \\right\\|}{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\|}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119566 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"}] :question/id #uuid "2db0218f-bfb3-552a-8683-2f32f230a3ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-3141" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(s) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s , \\: -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s, \\: \\sin s \\right\\rangle,\n\\quad 0\\leq s \\lt 2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\mathbf T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s,$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\| = \\| \\mathbf{r}''(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(s)$ and $\\mathbf r''(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6da15c27-0ab0-56cd-8ef3-27f8c1c55a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375925} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd2612d-5711-599a-a694-c2afac45f762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375926} {:answer/id #uuid "c63764c7-24ed-559f-b365-20b4780612bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{e}^{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375927} {:answer/id #uuid "a55dd6d8-17f7-5ead-b3ba-94f6823a5462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375928} {:answer/id #uuid "35aeb36f-92f3-56c9-80b5-a43746fc2a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da15c27-0ab0-56cd-8ef3-27f8c1c55a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375925} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d564c3b-bc44-527d-b38b-8c6df86c4124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fcaec574-ebde-5bb8-97c7-77da61871c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-131228" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{{e}^{t}},\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{{e}^{t}}⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{{e}^{t}})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{{e}^{t}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{e}^{2t}}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t}{{e}^{2t}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{e}^{t}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eac219c-4267-522b-be92-b62f92ac7ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3t}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264354} {:answer/id #uuid "e68618c1-a36d-5a2e-8722-fe2f8bcb89eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6t}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265007} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a88715-d9ff-5280-9ca0-7d4d09ce406e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265010} {:answer/id #uuid "ea457c6f-f692-586f-a47e-3cee22c3a295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265040} {:answer/id #uuid "eb89aad6-b8f7-5874-819d-e14ad0619362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6a88715-d9ff-5280-9ca0-7d4d09ce406e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265010} :answer-field/id #uuid "acc4f200-5c92-55c4-96c5-049c32e35817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ead3e0bf-d7e4-5bdd-88de-03a4e6ed527b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131230" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point $t>0$ on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨2t,\\,-3{t}^{2}⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}⟨3t,\\,2⟩,\\,t\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(3t)}^{2}+{(2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{9{t}^{2}+4} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+{(-3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6}{9{t}^{2}+4})}{t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03623963-16d7-553e-92b9-9f3efa2090ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443848} {:answer/id #uuid "55d8fe40-2fc5-5c9f-b218-ef946f9979e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443861} {:answer/id #uuid "87f377ec-25a7-5af0-9e08-2729d14d17c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443869} {:answer/id #uuid "a63b9eb5-9d48-5592-bb73-a581d4ffce7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443873} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d6f9ca-3714-5aa5-8b78-a6f173247922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03623963-16d7-553e-92b9-9f3efa2090ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443848} :answer-field/id #uuid "d272c7ef-b48e-5924-96ef-203f6d488dc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d152b171-fd28-5ce0-9099-77a199871a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131732" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=0$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,3⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{25}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10}),\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2}{25}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{25}⟨1,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12432056-a810-519c-9825-13b25ab2a228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443850} {:answer/id #uuid "2d492172-299d-5f9e-8553-a991858c87c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443854} {:answer/id #uuid "679116f9-97d1-5d62-a788-645a2d834296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443865} {:answer/id #uuid "ba97ff6b-bf06-5c94-b2f1-739a2843f441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443877} {:answer/id #uuid "cc70f6d3-c6fb-5244-881d-6bc189e3ab32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d492172-299d-5f9e-8553-a991858c87c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443854} :answer-field/id #uuid "c322fadd-ac27-57ed-bf43-9e8ac0bbc8e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e6f234b-737b-5376-aaeb-5d730bef9b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-131742" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s={\\pi }^{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s={\\pi }^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}({\\pi }^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ({\\pi }^{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}({\\pi }^{2})‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\cdot \\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206b9917-9249-5d96-885f-9052cced1472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443852} {:answer/id #uuid "38a62d49-ab80-5de1-b7d6-df3c195fadb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443856} {:answer/id #uuid "82909bce-1b68-5d11-be22-86b127324a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443868} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc52b86-edc3-5ab3-8c53-46f3784df89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443878} {:answer/id #uuid "e34cad78-7ce1-5b5b-aa1e-1145d9440cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "206b9917-9249-5d96-885f-9052cced1472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443852} :answer-field/id #uuid "e894091a-2e63-5373-8285-532c7e949b88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84ec701f-8d6f-546b-8f54-4258332a1413" :question/math-academy-id "q-131743" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-1⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖ \\\\  & =‖-\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5af6f583-3aa5-5c21-9b27-812d24aaba4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443863} {:answer/id #uuid "625782b0-4ad1-5de1-8987-e95b17c343ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443864} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a2861c-388d-58fc-af3f-6ca10eb128d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443872} {:answer/id #uuid "eda35170-2016-5f0d-84da-1b5c4583cefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443886} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f59c1d-0707-55ca-b46e-a15a0d3ed556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5af6f583-3aa5-5c21-9b27-812d24aaba4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443863} :answer-field/id #uuid "92b6ebf7-c2b9-5972-b09e-a6f7847a9371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d96a6265-af2d-5821-9fbc-e9e0d0216e3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131945" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\frac{4}{5}s⟩,\\,0\\le s<10\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{5}s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\frac{4}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{25}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{3}{25}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adad88a-ab1b-5262-9f58-e77aaec08261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{s}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266243} {:answer/id #uuid "411f2175-9bdc-56de-9535-626f1db416bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266731} {:answer/id #uuid "91be173e-099f-5c0e-be22-34b304fd7283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267440} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f9fbee-c825-5d6c-8b8b-ea7d62f0db9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267746} {:answer/id #uuid "e579c2d9-705c-540e-bad7-22f86cbdddc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2f9fbee-c825-5d6c-8b8b-ea7d62f0db9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267746} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c08d7bf-124f-5962-8d5b-721de0a87bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb73bb64-ede0-50a0-bba1-a62818a14994" :question/math-academy-id "q-132559" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨s-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡s,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({s}^{2}+1)⟩,\\,s\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({s}^{2}+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4s}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{2(1-{s}^{2})}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟨4s,\\,2(1-{s}^{2})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(4s)^{2}+{(2(1-{s}^{2}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{s}^{2}+4{s}^{4}-8{s}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{4{s}^{4}+8{s}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{4({s}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+1)}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be1ee9b-69bf-52e3-8089-48b6079a6650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411688} {:answer/id #uuid "6692c8a0-5b7a-50e2-8f3a-9789034d55a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411733} {:answer/id #uuid "9e30ff60-cfaf-503d-a59c-7208799a6d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411761} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e309d6-7791-565f-a947-86bc64e04da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411770} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c7f1db-e315-5925-b5d8-227085379706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0e309d6-7791-565f-a947-86bc64e04da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411770} :answer-field/id #uuid "008191e4-1343-56f9-9409-2e7c06d48454" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3fef8c5-dedd-5425-a060-104bbe0a3652" :question/math-academy-id "q-34177" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter t. Since we are given the curve r(t) parametrized by the parameter \nt (not the arc length s), we will use the following formula for the curvature\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ &  \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $t>0.$ \n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the curvature for  $t>0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cb19795-d34e-5eab-996c-a0750fdc83c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118096} {:answer/id #uuid "a4164bd7-cfc7-5984-a022-a3657f7c7aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118097} {:answer/id #uuid "d1087dd0-88f5-570e-9a06-92ad31fd2f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118098} {:answer/id #uuid "f392ca45-fded-5387-970f-6c0e65df7b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118099} {:answer/id #uuid "418dcfbf-c00e-53c1-9492-73920469e660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f392ca45-fded-5387-970f-6c0e65df7b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118099} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7bbcb5c-6f44-588f-a8d6-899a42547484" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4aa7d1da-7858-5140-849b-d462fe65d915" :question/math-academy-id "q-34355" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}},\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩,\\,0\\le s<2\\sqrt{10}\\,\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}},\\,-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨1,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1),\\,-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨0,\\,-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}))}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\sqrt{0+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{10}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b00855ab-cf4f-598c-98e3-70f570e975f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119079} {:answer/id #uuid "de4ddacb-de2e-506b-9cd6-ca31cbd7387e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119080} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec4d528-3865-566e-b0f2-7928ad804460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119081} {:answer/id #uuid "71eb4d9d-bf87-5ee1-bab6-0262a42b7b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119082} {:answer/id #uuid "73cab0bc-9afb-5a1a-827a-444f5929111e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de4ddacb-de2e-506b-9cd6-ca31cbd7387e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119080} :answer-field/id #uuid "058516c5-41da-5120-8490-39e6081e2067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff2e0fe9-5f3d-51ba-a9a0-292022683d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-64584" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{3},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a3aa75-660c-575d-82d3-d2c2e0ba5b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333037} {:answer/id #uuid "08550f3e-58a7-5558-9ee9-f59ca8cf9e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333069} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5a98c6-f26e-5720-87d6-4668e8efbc20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333416} {:answer/id #uuid "756b6572-d426-55d5-8a1f-860fff859319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334048} {:answer/id #uuid "cb26701c-39d6-5b44-91a1-7766d3a0f3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08550f3e-58a7-5558-9ee9-f59ca8cf9e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333069} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb69352-4149-593c-bc7d-4e7284e4e477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e18d5a8-08c4-5591-8e9a-7f22a6b8acbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-64661" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+2\\,j-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization And the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be96d5c-0914-5fe5-acba-da0c7e6d8b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443853} {:answer/id #uuid "5562ffbc-ebce-5ef5-a7e7-e05b1cb533d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443860} {:answer/id #uuid "5616aca8-3b97-5fdd-9cff-fae082d196cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443862} {:answer/id #uuid "9372156d-f747-53e5-bf4d-3dde0aba7079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443871} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a83a8d-c1c5-5b09-a81e-6dcef9136233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9372156d-f747-53e5-bf4d-3dde0aba7079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443871} :answer-field/id #uuid "70818e4d-0bd1-5756-b56e-538edbd5bffe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4f686a5-889f-5e90-8c7e-36ce4fec4b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-80521" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=2{\\pi }^{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n \n\n$$\nT(s)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=2{\\pi }^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}}{\\sqrt{2s}}\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}}{\\sqrt{2s}}\\,j \\\\ {T}^{′}(2{\\pi }^{2}) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}{\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}{\\sqrt{2(2{\\pi }^{2})}}\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,i+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(2{\\pi }^{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(2{\\pi }^{2})‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2\\pi })}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f54c52e-665b-579e-86df-670272b9e806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443851} {:answer/id #uuid "3260ca78-14a6-50d0-b36b-a07da635b595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443855} {:answer/id #uuid "68140ba3-9983-541d-b347-0a33e474e0b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443866} {:answer/id #uuid "7429db73-b111-5e68-a8d3-3a5b83ea06db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443867} {:answer/id #uuid "ba467f5e-b778-5059-b612-0bd7bb8b3015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba467f5e-b778-5059-b612-0bd7bb8b3015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443876} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6c859aa-2556-59ff-a25e-6af1968d5cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4a4a281-bd0c-502e-a09a-cc4e77ac53a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-83643" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where:\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{3-8s}{10},\\,\\frac{6s+4}{10}⟩,\\,s\\ge 0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3-8s}{10}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{6s+4}{10})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{8}{10},\\,\\frac{6}{10}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b5588c5-37db-5b02-87d7-05e19f211482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443849} {:answer/id #uuid "50a64c5e-ee2e-5e33-99cd-2507a3e15ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443859} {:answer/id #uuid "db8aafa7-86be-5335-ad0b-879f8daf56c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443882} {:answer/id #uuid "df3fead8-a8d0-5dc8-8d4a-f1f7b93d5a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443883} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f51edd-60f6-5c7d-8ca5-c07095020041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b5588c5-37db-5b02-87d7-05e19f211482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443849} :answer-field/id #uuid "92c3c624-d0ce-5d7e-af1f-33bffa533d5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e84a8d6-a1ed-5f78-832b-753ef57840b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-83657" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,3-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩,\\,0\\le s<8\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{4}|\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curvature Given a General Parametrization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9b736d-97b9-5346-ae4c-3f48e12a4b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443857} {:answer/id #uuid "4efce17f-3075-5e92-ad94-a11200baf0b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443858} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0a7ca2-651b-528e-afe7-bc816f290417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443870} {:answer/id #uuid "ac11b4df-2cb6-5f6b-92fb-3e07ba50cb5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443875} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b8e622-9766-5512-823c-41c899359c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c9b736d-97b9-5346-ae4c-3f48e12a4b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443857} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ae9bf6-e514-5558-98b8-e081859740e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "941975f4-ea50-5edb-a299-e8568f71e188" :question/math-academy-id "q-83663" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\,-12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})i+12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3})\\,j,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}+{(12{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12{t}^{2})^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+(12{t}^{2})^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(12{t}^{2})^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3}))} \\\\  & =12{t}^{2} \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}+{(-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3{t}^{2})^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+(-3{t}^{2})^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{3})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{3}))} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{12{t}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
